# Standard propositional operators over every tetra pair. These must always
# yield true/false; both/neither may be inputs but must never leak into the
# result. Paradoxical operators (and, or, not) are exercised in logic.doxa.
(true xor true)?
(true xor false)?
(true xor both)?
(true xor neither)?
(false xor true)?
(false xor false)?
(false xor both)?
(false xor neither)?
(both xor true)?
(both xor false)?
(both xor both)?
(both xor neither)?
(neither xor true)?
(neither xor false)?
(neither xor both)?
(neither xor neither)?
(true implies true)?
(true implies false)?
(true implies both)?
(true implies neither)?
(false implies true)?
(false implies false)?
(false implies both)?
(false implies neither)?
(both implies true)?
(both implies false)?
(both implies both)?
(both implies neither)?
(neither implies true)?
(neither implies false)?
(neither implies both)?
(neither implies neither)?
(true iff true)?
(true iff false)?
(true iff both)?
(true iff neither)?
(false iff true)?
(false iff false)?
(false iff both)?
(false iff neither)?
(both iff true)?
(both iff false)?
(both iff both)?
(both iff neither)?
(neither iff true)?
(neither iff false)?
(neither iff both)?
(neither iff neither)?
(true nand true)?
(true nand false)?
(true nand both)?
(true nand neither)?
(false nand true)?
(false nand false)?
(false nand both)?
(false nand neither)?
(both nand true)?
(both nand false)?
(both nand both)?
(both nand neither)?
(neither nand true)?
(neither nand false)?
(neither nand both)?
(neither nand neither)?
(true nor true)?
(true nor false)?
(true nor both)?
(true nor neither)?
(false nor true)?
(false nor false)?
(false nor both)?
(false nor neither)?
(both nor true)?
(both nor false)?
(both nor both)?
(both nor neither)?
(neither nor true)?
(neither nor false)?
(neither nor both)?
(neither nor neither)?
